"To determine the number of vertical asymptotes of the graph of \\( y = \\frac{2}{x^2+x-6} \\), we need to find the values of \\( x \\) that make the denominator zero, as vertical asymptotes occur where the function is undefined.\n\nThe denominator of the function is \\( x^2 + x - 6 \\). We set this equal to zero and solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ x^2 + x - 6 = 0 \\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation, and we can factor it:\n\n\\[ (x + 3)(x - 2) = 0 \\]\n\nSetting each factor equal to zero gives us the solutions:\n\n\\[ x + 3 = 0 \\implies x = -3 \\]\n\n\\[ x - 2 = 0 \\implies x = 2 \\]\n\nTherefore, the function has vertical asymptotes at \\( x = -3 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\).\n\nThus, the number of vertical asymptotes is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."
"We can pair the given sums as follows:\n\\begin{align*}\na+b&=10,\na+c&=18,\na+d&=19,\nb+c&=20,\nb+d&=21,\nc+d&=29.\n\\end{align*}\nAdding all these equations, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n2a+2b+2c+2d&=10+18+19+20+21+29\\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\qquad 2(a+b+c+d)&=117\n\\Rightarrow\\qquad a+b+c+d&=58.5\n\\end{align*}\nSince $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ are distinct integers, we can conclude that $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ must be $1$, $2$, $3$, and $52$, respectively. Therefore, the four integers in increasing order are $\\boxed{1,2,3,52}$."
"To find \\( f(-10) \\), we need to determine which piece of the piecewise function to use. The function \\( f(x) \\) is defined as:\n\n\\[\nf(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\n3x + 5 & \\text{if } x < -3, \\\\\n7 - 4x & \\text{if } x \\ge -3.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSince \\( -10 < -3 \\), we use the first piece of the function:\n\n\\[\nf(x) = 3x + 5.\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( x = -10 \\) into the function:\n\n\\[\nf(-10) = 3(-10) + 5 = -30 + 5 = -25.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(-10) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-25}\\)."
"To evaluate the expression \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\) when \\(a = 5\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify the expression \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\) by adding the exponents.\n2. Substitute \\(a = 5\\) into the simplified expression.\n\nFirst, simplify the expression:\n\\[\na^3 \\cdot a^2 = a^{3+2} = a^5\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(a = 5\\) into the simplified expression:\n\\[\na^5 = 5^5\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate \\(5^5\\):\n\\[\n5^5 = 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 = 3125\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\) when \\(a = 5\\) is \\(\\boxed{3125}\\)."
