"To evaluate \\(\\log_3 81\\), we need to determine the exponent to which 3 must be raised to obtain 81. In other words, we need to solve the equation:\n\n\\[ 3^x = 81\\]\n\nWe know that 81 can be expressed as a power of 3:\n\n\\[ 81 = 3^4\\]\n\nSo, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[ 3^x = 3^4\\]\n\nSince the bases are the same, we can set the exponents equal to each other:\n\n\\[ x = 4\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\log_3 81\\) is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{4}\\]"
"To find the sum of all the counting numbers in column E, we need to identify the pattern in the column. Column E consists of the numbers 5, 6, 15, 16, ..., 50. This is an arithmetic sequence where the first term is 5 and the common difference is 1.\n\nThe number of terms in this sequence can be found by dividing the last term by the first term by the common difference and adding 1:\n\\[\n\\frac{50 - 5}{1} + 1 = 46\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by the formula:\n\\[\nS = \\frac{n}{2} \\times (\\text{first term} + \\text{last term})\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[\nS = \\frac{46}{2} \\times (5 + 50) = 23 \\times 55 = 1215\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of all the counting numbers in column E is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1215}\n\\]"
