"To determine the probability that the top card is a face card, we first need to count the total number of face cards in a standard deck of 52 cards.\n\nA face card is a Jack, Queen, or King. There are 3 face cards in each suit, and there are 4 suits in a deck. Therefore, the total number of face cards is:\n\n\\[ 3 \\text{ face cards per suit} \\times 4 \\text{ suits} = 12 \\text{ face cards} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the probability by drawing a face card from a deck of 52 cards. The probability \\( P \\) is given by the ratio of the number of face cards to the total number of cards in the deck:\n\n\\[ P = \\frac{\\text{Number of face cards}}{\\text{Total number of cards}} = \\frac{12}{52} = \\frac{3}{13} \\]\n\nThus, the probability that the top card is a face card is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{13}}\\)."
