"To determine the number of interior diagonals in a regular nine-sided polygon, we can use the formula for the number of diagonals in an polygon with \\( n \\) sides. The formula is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{n(n-3)}{2}\n\\]\n\nFor a nine-sided polygon, \\( n = 9 \\). Plugging \\( n into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{9(9-3)}{2} = \\frac{9 \\times 6}{2} = \\frac{54}{2} = 27\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of interior diagonals in a regular nine-sided polygon is \\(\\boxed{27}\\)."
"To determine how many times all three lights will come on at the same time during a seven-minute dance, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their blinking intervals. The blinking intervals are 2 seconds, 3 seconds, and 5 seconds.\n\nFirst, we find the LCM of 2 and 3:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(2, 3) = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the LCM of 6 and 5:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(6, 5) = 30\n\\]\n\nThus, the LCM of 2, 3, and 5 is 30 seconds.\n\nNow, we need to determine how many times 30 seconds fits into 420 seconds (since 7 minutes is 420 seconds):\n\\[\n\\frac{420}{30} = 14\n\\]\n\nTherefore, all three lights will come on at the same time 14 times during a seven-minute dance.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $\\boxed{14}$."
