"To determine the height of the tree, we can use the concept of similar triangles. The woman and her shadow form one triangle, and the tree and its shadow form another triangle. Since the sun's rays are parallel, these triangles are similar.\n\nLet's denote the height of the tree by \\( h \\) feet. The ratio of the height of the woman to the length of her shadow is the same as the ratio of the height of the tree to the length of its shadow. Therefore, we can write the following proportion:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{h}{120}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( h \\), we can cross-multiply:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 120 = 8 \\times h\n\\]\n\n\\[\n600 = 8h\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh = \\frac{600}{8}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh = 75\n\\]\n\nThus, the height of the tree is \\(\\boxed{75}\\) feet."
