"To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 315 and 108, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of 0.\n\n1. Divide 315 by 108 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   315 \\div 108 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 9\n   \\]\n   So, \\(315 = 108 \\cdot 3 + 9\\).\n\n2. Now, divide 108 by 9 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   108 \\div 9 = 12 \\text{ remainder } 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(108 = 9 \\cdot 12 + 0\\).\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, the GCD is the last non-zero remainder, which is 9.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 315 and 108 is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."
